{"name":"Eagles Nest","hex":"#8a693f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eagles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of eagle"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of eagle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eagles"},{"term":"nest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure built by a bird as a place to incubate eggs and rear young.","Any of various similar structures or sites used by other animals:\nA structure built, or site modified, to incubate eggs, rear young, or shelter a colony."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build or settle into a nest.","To settle into a home."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eaglenest Range","blocks":[{"text":"The Eaglenest Range is a mountain range on the west side of the Spatsizi Plateau in northern British Columbia, Canada. It has an area of 2448 km2 and is a subrange of the Interior Mountains which in turn form part of the Pacific Cordillera mountain system."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eaglenest_Range"},{"title":"Eagle's Nest Park","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle's Nest Park is a scenic lookout in the town of Bancroft, Ontario, Canada. It is built on the top of a sheer rock face and overlooks the northern portions of the town, the York River and Bancroft Airport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Viewing_platform_in_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg/330px-Viewing_platform_in_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle's_Nest_Park"},{"title":"Eagles Nest (Colorado)","blocks":[{"text":"Eagles Nest is a 13,419-foot (4,090 m) mountain summit in Summit County, Colorado, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Eagles_Nest%2C_Colorado.jpg/330px-Eagles_Nest%2C_Colorado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagles_Nest_(Colorado)"},{"title":"Eagle","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle is the common name for certain large predatory birds of prey within the family of the Accipitridae. While on a genetic level, only the subfamily Aquilinae comprises \"true eagles\", many other species are commonly referred to as eagles, such as the bald eagle, and the term generally carries no taxonomic weight. Most of the 68 species of eagles are from Eurasia and Africa. Outside this area, just 14 species can be found—two in North America, nine in Central and South America, and three in Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Eagles_together.jpg/330px-Eagles_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg/500px-The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg/1280px-The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg/500px-The_sheer_rock_of_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park_facing_Hastings_St.-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sheer rock of Eagle's Nest Park facing Hastings St.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_sheer